WEBVTT

00:06.717 --> 00:09.867
The Tus militia has been defeated
by the nomads.

00:10.407 --> 00:11.957
With our forces wiped out,

00:11.957 --> 00:15.557
it will be difficult to prevent them
from entering the city.

00:16.547 --> 00:18.457
When they arrive, there will be pillaging.

00:18.707 --> 00:21.507
Let's hide all of our food
and valuables before then.

00:24.807 --> 00:26.887
Not much will fit down here.

00:36.727 --> 00:40.367
I will lead my sons to the mountains
 to take shelter.

00:40.367 --> 00:42.427
Yes, that is a good idea.

00:42.427 --> 00:45.967
You and Sitara should hide
 in the cellar, Fatima.

00:46.767 --> 00:48.497
We will come for you in three days.

00:48.817 --> 00:51.367
Sitara, I leave Fatima in your hands.

00:51.687 --> 00:53.787
Right. I will keep her safe.

00:54.017 --> 00:56.427
Until then, Mistress and Sitara.

00:56.427 --> 00:57.747
See you soon.

00:58.997 --> 01:04.357
This takes me back to my childhood. 
We fled our city countless times.

01:04.357 --> 01:07.817
You should at least show
a little bit of concern.

01:14.777 --> 01:17.557
Here, Mistress. Have some dates.

01:18.527 --> 01:20.517
Thank you, Sitara.

01:22.697 --> 01:26.987
Being down here, it almost feels
like time has stood still.

01:27.837 --> 01:32.447
The outside light that can be seen through
 here has come and gone three times.

01:33.207 --> 01:36.367
Uncle and the others 
will come for us soon.

01:36.967 --> 01:39.537
And even if they take
a little longer than expected,

01:39.977 --> 01:44.077
thanks to their foresight,
we have the supplies to see us through.

01:44.077 --> 01:46.177
And your precious books are safe, too.

01:46.177 --> 01:47.087
That's true.

01:47.547 --> 01:51.257
Thank you, Sitara. Having you with me
 has kept my spirits up.

01:51.257 --> 01:54.507
Oh, I haven't done anything.

01:55.847 --> 02:00.817
Come to think of it, Mistress, 
do you think the nomads read Euclid?

02:01.187 --> 02:02.787
I haven't the slightest idea.

02:02.787 --> 02:05.887
But I mustn't lose a single one.

02:05.887 --> 02:08.607
My husband spent his life
collecting these volumes.

02:09.597 --> 02:10.867
Yes, you're right.

02:11.747 --> 02:13.577
So tell me, Sitara.

02:14.587 --> 02:16.407
Do you care for Muhammad?

02:19.597 --> 02:22.627
Um, yes. I hold him 
in the highest regard.

02:22.947 --> 02:25.877
There can't be many in this world
 as intelligent as him.

02:27.727 --> 02:29.867
He takes after his father.

02:30.247 --> 02:33.717
He always bridled at the restrictions
of conservative theology.

02:35.647 --> 02:39.367
The more he goes down 
his own path in life,

02:39.367 --> 02:42.267
the more resistance 
he will meet, I'm sure of it.

02:42.777 --> 02:46.827
In such times, only one person will 
be able to offer him support and comfort.

02:48.347 --> 02:50.757
Sitara, that person is you.

02:52.287 --> 02:54.447
I want you to serve him at his side.

02:54.717 --> 02:56.657
As a human being.

03:18.937 --> 03:19.877
I will.

03:28.737 --> 03:30.297
It's my brother and the girls.

03:30.297 --> 03:32.237
We can finally come out.

03:32.237 --> 03:33.087
Yes.

04:11.057 --> 04:12.557
Ah.

04:22.887 --> 04:25.577
<b>Jaadugar</b>

05:52.127 --> 05:57.357
<b>The Roses That Bloom in Safar</b>

05:56.247 --> 05:57.547
Thank you, Sitara.

05:57.547 --> 05:58.567
Not at all.

05:59.677 --> 06:00.717
Stand aside.

06:04.907 --> 06:05.677
Sitara.

06:06.077 --> 06:07.697
Don't offer any resistance.

06:09.907 --> 06:12.037
Yes, Mistress.

06:30.227 --> 06:31.897
<i>Highness! I've found it!</i>

06:36.567 --> 06:37.727
<i>This is it.</i>

06:44.067 --> 06:45.027
<i>Hmm...</i>

06:45.987 --> 06:48.577
<i>So this is Euclid's </i>Elements<i>.</i>

06:50.967 --> 06:52.897
No. Not that book.

06:58.457 --> 06:59.627
<i>You're certain?</i>

07:00.337 --> 07:01.507
<i>Y-Yes, Highness!</i>

07:03.177 --> 07:04.137
<i>Ha ha ha!</i>

07:04.467 --> 07:06.577
<i>Then it was worth coming all this way.</i>

07:07.807 --> 07:09.887
<i>What of the other books, sire?</i>

07:14.147 --> 07:16.607
<i>I've no need of them. Do with them as you wish.</i>

07:17.357 --> 07:17.857
<i>Sire.</i>

07:27.297 --> 07:30.807
"Cut off the hands of thieves,
whether they be man or woman,

07:30.807 --> 07:33.567
as punishment for what they have done!"

07:34.267 --> 07:35.097
Sitara!

07:35.097 --> 07:39.417
That book doesn't belong
 to you! Give it back!

07:39.747 --> 07:40.667
<i>What did she say?</i>

07:41.167 --> 07:42.217
<i>Um...</i>

07:43.087 --> 07:46.217
<i>She said you should return the stolen book, sire.</i>

07:47.347 --> 07:49.347
<i>You malign me as a thief?</i>

07:51.807 --> 07:52.747
<i>You are mistaken.</i>

07:53.557 --> 07:54.957
<i>As the sun touches the whole world,</i>

07:55.477 --> 08:00.317
<i>so everything on it belongs to my father,
 the great Genghis Khan!</i>

08:00.947 --> 08:02.247
"I am no thief."

08:02.597 --> 08:04.297
"Everything on this Earth..."

08:04.297 --> 08:07.347
"...belongs to my master's father, 
the great Genghis Khan."

08:04.797 --> 08:07.347
<i>This boy understands our language.</i>

08:07.587 --> 08:09.257
So says my master.

08:10.287 --> 08:11.327
<i>Girl.</i>

08:12.407 --> 08:14.307
<i>You are quite the brave one, aren't you?</i>

08:16.287 --> 08:17.517
<i>It is unseemly.</i>

08:18.287 --> 08:19.587
<i>A delicate thing like you</i>

08:20.087 --> 08:21.707
<i>should know but one thing.</i>

08:23.297 --> 08:24.277
<i>And that is fear.</i>

08:27.387 --> 08:27.907
No.

08:51.417 --> 08:53.827
M-Mistress?

08:59.497 --> 09:00.837
Don't you...

09:02.107 --> 09:03.317
dare touch...

09:07.477 --> 09:09.537
...my daughter.

09:13.667 --> 09:14.997
Mistress?

09:15.577 --> 09:16.827
Mistress?

09:16.827 --> 09:18.287
Mistress!

10:52.497 --> 10:53.657
Sitara?

11:00.397 --> 11:01.517
You're alive.

11:02.577 --> 11:03.657
Are you hurt?

11:05.147 --> 11:06.387
Ms. Anis.

11:06.837 --> 11:07.727
I...

11:08.727 --> 11:12.297
I didn't keep my promise...

11:13.167 --> 11:15.557
to keep the mistress safe.

11:15.557 --> 11:16.927
The mistress is...

11:18.527 --> 11:19.587
I see.

11:23.317 --> 11:27.677
We were captured on our way
 to the mountains.

11:32.087 --> 11:35.887
After that, we were divided into groups.

11:36.547 --> 11:40.407
Women, children, and skilled craftsmen.

11:41.007 --> 11:45.917
The rest, the men and the elderly, 
were all taken away somewhere.

11:46.747 --> 11:48.457
That was the last time we saw Uncle.

11:51.477 --> 11:52.857
Not long after...

11:57.387 --> 11:58.537
Mikhail!

12:08.637 --> 12:09.587
Mikhail!

12:12.347 --> 12:13.297
No...

12:14.507 --> 12:16.187
Ms. Zumurrud...

12:16.987 --> 12:18.067
<i>Get up!</i>

12:18.737 --> 12:19.777
<i>We're leaving!</i>

12:24.637 --> 12:28.037
Please stop crying. Be a good baby.

12:28.987 --> 12:30.567
Ms. Zumurrud.

12:30.567 --> 12:32.007
Can you stand?

12:34.927 --> 12:36.057
Have you got her?

12:46.217 --> 12:47.207
<i>I know that man.</i>

12:47.807 --> 12:51.167
<i>He's the ironmonger who fixed
that water bucket all those years ago.</i>

12:52.777 --> 12:55.277
<i>We have to find Uncle 
and the others quickly.</i>

13:04.277 --> 13:06.387
Hasan! Hasan!

13:12.027 --> 13:12.757
Chuu!

13:16.417 --> 13:19.387
<i>Their fear of these mysterious men</i>

13:19.387 --> 13:22.097
<i>spurred Sitara and the others
into the wasteland.</i>

13:28.497 --> 13:32.337
<i>The month of Safar this year
is still a little chilly,</i>

13:32.337 --> 13:33.977
<i>so the water's cold.</i>

13:36.487 --> 13:41.907
<i>But when the sun is out, 
I spy the rosebuds already swelling.</i>

13:46.117 --> 13:48.647
<i>As we do our chores...</i>

13:48.647 --> 13:55.417
"In the name of Allah,
the most Gracious, the Most Merciful."

13:52.807 --> 13:56.857
<i>...we can hear Uncle's students
practicing their recitation.</i>

13:57.487 --> 13:59.057
Isn't that adorable?

13:59.867 --> 14:02.327
It reminds me of when I first came here.

14:04.487 --> 14:06.077
They've returned!

14:08.167 --> 14:10.587
Welcome home, Mistress.

14:10.587 --> 14:12.487
How did it go at the bazaar?

14:12.487 --> 14:16.137
Thanks to Zumurrud,
I found lots of great bargains.

14:16.137 --> 14:18.927
I'm always at your service, Mistress.

14:19.637 --> 14:20.577
That's true.

14:21.337 --> 14:24.077
You'll have to come with us
 next time, Sitara.

14:24.077 --> 14:24.867
Okay.

14:24.867 --> 14:25.467
Sitara.

14:26.117 --> 14:28.227
I sent a letter off to Nishapur.

14:28.657 --> 14:31.797
A reply might arrive by the time
 the roses are in bloom.

14:34.767 --> 14:39.587
<i>After the month of Safar comes the month
of Rabi' al-Awwal, when the roses bloom.</i>

14:40.497 --> 14:42.467
<i>Or rather, when they should have.</i>

14:52.757 --> 14:54.137
Zumurrud.

14:54.137 --> 14:56.537
You must eat something
to keep up your energy.

14:58.217 --> 15:00.507
You need to eat, too, Sitara.

15:01.237 --> 15:03.087
You eat it, Ms. Anis.

15:04.507 --> 15:05.537
Thank you.

15:06.217 --> 15:08.977
But this is your share.

15:10.177 --> 15:12.057
Hey, do you remember?

15:13.157 --> 15:17.597
When I said that slaves don't get
to decide anything for themselves?

15:19.827 --> 15:20.487
Yes.

15:20.727 --> 15:22.417
If you look at it another way,

15:22.767 --> 15:26.327
it also means slaves aren't
 responsible for anything.

15:27.167 --> 15:31.027
For instance, if a slave commits a crime,

15:31.027 --> 15:33.917
their punishment is only half 
that of a free man.

15:34.907 --> 15:40.377
You might say we aren't considered 
capable of responsibility for our actions.

15:41.787 --> 15:43.157
What happened to the mistress...

15:43.607 --> 15:47.427
You mustn't decide for yourself whether
 you were responsible for it or not.

15:49.147 --> 15:51.807
Then, who gets to decide it?

15:52.637 --> 15:54.467
There's no one left who can.

15:54.827 --> 15:57.887
Not the mistress. Nor Uncle.
 They're both...

15:59.117 --> 16:00.127
That's true.

16:01.457 --> 16:02.237
Actually, no.

16:03.107 --> 16:06.477
There is still one person. In Nishapur.

16:12.637 --> 16:14.167
Master Muhammad...

16:17.487 --> 16:21.337
Master Muhammad is still alive.

16:22.637 --> 16:23.547
That's right.

16:23.957 --> 16:27.137
We still have one thing to believe in.

16:38.967 --> 16:39.687
We...

16:42.267 --> 16:43.247
We do!

16:47.187 --> 16:52.787
<i>After that, the prisoners 
continued eastward, day after day.</i>

16:55.557 --> 17:02.897
<b>Tus</b>

16:55.557 --> 17:02.897
<b>Taloqan</b>

16:57.187 --> 17:02.007
<i>They threaded their way between mountains,
 crossed rivers, and then...</i>

17:02.847 --> 17:05.297
<i>Just as the month of Safar was ending...</i>

17:06.237 --> 17:07.197
<i>Get out!</i>

17:11.747 --> 17:18.827
<i>...the caravan arrived at a group of tents
pitched in a place called Taloqan.</i>

17:28.447 --> 17:31.137
<i>There are people here who aren't soldiers.</i>

17:31.137 --> 17:33.157
<i>Could this be their city?</i>

17:34.447 --> 17:35.617
Excuse me.

17:35.617 --> 17:37.447
Where are you from?

17:38.717 --> 17:39.837
From Tus.

17:41.567 --> 17:43.547
I can't believe it.
They've even sacked Tus?

17:44.477 --> 17:46.007
Where are you from?

17:46.297 --> 17:49.487
We were spared when we told them
 we were skilled craftsmen,

17:49.487 --> 17:51.567
and we were brought here.

17:53.947 --> 17:55.517
We're from Nishapur.

17:58.277 --> 18:02.967
Learning of the approach of the nomads, 
we fortified our defenses.

18:06.617 --> 18:12.647
And when they finally appeared, 
an arrow fired from the ramparts

18:13.137 --> 18:16.347
struck their commander true.

18:20.187 --> 18:26.227
And for that single arrow, Nishapur 
was burned to the ground in retaliation.

18:28.687 --> 18:32.027
<i>Mav Baliq, the Bad Town,
spilled the blood of my blood.</i>

18:32.817 --> 18:38.867
<i>Kill every living thing your eyes fall upon.
Spare nothing. Not a single dog or bird.</i>

18:39.907 --> 18:42.907
We craftsmen are the only survivors.

18:42.907 --> 18:45.607
Everyone else, even the women
and children, were...

18:48.497 --> 18:51.367
<i>Master Muhammad was in Nishapur.</i>

18:57.987 --> 18:59.497
This can't be...

19:02.507 --> 19:03.767
Zumurrud!

19:04.997 --> 19:06.187
Ms. Zumurrud!

19:09.387 --> 19:11.557
Mikhail.

19:13.957 --> 19:15.347
Zumurrud.

19:16.207 --> 19:18.307
The setting sun.

19:18.307 --> 19:23.077
Ah, it's so bright, isn't it, Mikhail?

19:26.427 --> 19:29.267
It's so beautiful.

19:32.277 --> 19:33.567
Ms. Zumurrud!

19:33.567 --> 19:34.707
Don't.

19:35.157 --> 19:36.657
Don't leave us.

19:37.317 --> 19:38.767
I beg you.

19:39.847 --> 19:44.127
Ms. Zumurrud came from a foreign land
where she could see the sea.

19:45.257 --> 19:48.497
She served the mistress 
longer than any of us.

19:49.927 --> 19:54.067
Did she actually want to return
to her homeland that whole time?

19:54.827 --> 19:57.757
Did she miss her family that whole time?

20:01.057 --> 20:05.437
Let us at least give her a proper burial,

20:05.687 --> 20:09.027
so she can be reunited
 with her little brother.

20:10.547 --> 20:13.947
<i>"Indeed, we belong to Allah...</i>

20:13.947 --> 20:17.987
<i>and indeed, to Him we shall return."</i>

20:13.947 --> 20:17.987
"...and indeed, to Him we shall return."

20:33.057 --> 20:35.837
Now there is nothing that sparks joy.

20:45.087 --> 20:46.457
Poor thing.

20:46.457 --> 20:47.717
What happened?

20:49.967 --> 20:51.207
Excuse me.

20:53.227 --> 20:55.857
She lunged at a soldier 
who was walking by.

20:56.237 --> 20:58.557
He struck her down on the spot.

20:58.557 --> 21:00.027
How dreadful.

21:00.027 --> 21:02.587
Why is everyone...

21:04.897 --> 21:07.367
Peace be upon her soul.

21:08.937 --> 21:11.147
<i>She decided it for herself.</i>

21:11.697 --> 21:16.707
<i>Rather than becoming 
a slave to the nomads,</i>

21:16.707 --> 21:21.597
<i>Ms. Anis wanted to die
a slave to her Tus family.</i>

21:26.177 --> 21:27.387
<i>I know.</i>

21:27.777 --> 21:33.567
<i>If I keep walking straight ahead,
maybe someone will shoot an arrow into me.</i>

21:39.147 --> 21:40.037
Wait!

21:42.927 --> 21:44.287
<i>It's the boy who...</i>

21:50.387 --> 21:51.917
Ow. It's...

21:52.637 --> 21:54.627
It's not... I-It's not like that!

21:54.947 --> 21:56.087
Hey! Listen!

21:56.387 --> 21:58.457
Don't you want to get that book back?

22:05.977 --> 22:07.057
Huh?

23:38.067 --> 23:43.257
<b>An Undying Flame</b>

23:38.477 --> 23:41.247
<i>Next time: "An Undying Flame."</i>
